  "slug": "microbe-comprehensive-mapping-583d",
  "summary": "Bacterial genome mapping now spans metabolic models, interactomes, and proteome annotation, extending function assignment across strains and species.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is scaling bacterial functional annotation and mapping across genomes, strains and species. Genome-scale metabolic models of 550 soil MAG-derived organisms use FBA to predict conserved amino acid and fermentation fluxes across phylogeny. A dual-sgRNA CRISPRi platform with barcoded pairs maps essential-gene genetic interactions in M. smegmatis and M. tuberculosis. DeepEST combines expression, operon-aware gene location and predicted structures to assign GO terms, while ContextMirror2.0 predicts species-specific interactomes for E. coli, S. enterica and S. aureus from sequence coevolution. A whole-proteome pipeline annotates E. coli UTI89, surfacing host-microbe and microbe-phage pathways. Sourmash k-mer profiling of long-read metagenome mock communities recovers gene content with F1 0.942 to 0.998. What is new in these items is the pairing of learned or sequence-based predictors with mechanistic and experimental layers to assign function at proteome and community scale.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-09"
}
